    "body": "Big Buck Bunny, I see you!\n\nDo you know what the adaptive formats supported by browser are, is it just HLS or are there more? It's an interesting idea to give the user control over the bitrate in these scenarios. In principle there is nothing preventing the built-in `<video controls>` from exposing such a menu today, but do you mean added APIs on `HTMLMediaElement` so that script-created controls can also show such a menu?\n",
