    "body": "> Big Buck Bunny, I see you!\n\nGood eye :) \n\n>  is it just HLS or are there more?\n\nDASH can also be configured to support client-driven adaptive streaming. I haven't experimented much with it personally but [IE11 on Win8.1+](https://blogs.msdn.microsoft.com/ie/2015/01/29/simplified-adaptive-video-streaming-announcing-support-for-hls-and-dash-in-windows-10/) claims native DASH support.\n\n> do you mean added APIs on HTMLMediaElement so that script-created controls can also show such a menu?\n\nYes, that's what I was thinking. Looking over the current state of the media element API, it seems really close to being able to provide this capability through Video/AudioTrackLists. If it were possible for application developers to change [selectedIndex](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-videotracklist-selectedindex), for instance, I think that could be used to build a custom quality selector control.\n",
