    "body": "It is possible to change the selected video track, by setting [`VideoTrack.selected`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-videotrack-selected). This will implicitly deselect all other video tracks. However, there are a few problems:\n1. As you have no doubt noticed, the audio/video tracks APIs are not widely implemented yet.\n2. With adaptive streaming, there is conceptually still only one video track. Presumably it's possible to have multi-angle video also with HLS or DASH, so there would have to be some way of grouping together video tracks that are conceptually the same.\n\nImplementation is just a matter of time/priorities, but I'm not sure what to do about the second issue.\n\nIs this something you want for video.js, and is it for mobile browsers that support HLS? At least in the case of Android, HLS is implemented by the OS outside of the browser's direct control, so I'm not certain that the APIs even exist to achieve the level of control needed for this:\nhttp://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaPlayer.html\n\nI assume that you have investigated using Media Source Extensions to implement HLS or DASH in the browser, but that the same-origin policy ruins it for you? If not, that would really allow all the flexibility you want.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
