    "created_at": "2016-02-02T06:42:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-02T06:42:38Z",
    "body": "Since all bitrates of the same logical video track would have the same metadata, I'm thinking that if this were to be exposed, some extension to `VideoTrack` would work. Something like\n\n``` WebIDL\npartial interface VideoTrack {\n  sequence<double> getAvailableBitrates();\n  // promise resolves when change has taken effect\n  Promise<void> setPreferredBitrate(double bitrate);\n};\n```\n\nThe `VideoTracks` interface itself isn't shipping in Chromium yet, but I see that Safari has it. @jernoble, is this something you've had requests for? What would make sense?\n\n@dmlap, you mention Flash. Can this be done today using Flash, and if so do you know what Flash's API for doing this looks like?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
