    "created_at": "2016-02-03T04:08:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-03T04:08:42Z",
    "body": "Flash's `play2()` sounds like it's the Flash API that MSE was intended to replace, in that it's a more low-level \"stitch together these streams\" API than a high-level \"use this quality level from the manifest.\"\n\nYour `getAvailableRepresentations()` proposal would most likely work, in that it's always possible to use _some_ string. Do DASH and HLS always have unique string for each representation, or could it be necessary for the implementation to generate a string? If it is, then this would be a bit more work, in that people could then depend on how the string is generated and how to parse the bitrate/resolution from that string.\n\n@jernoble, given that Safari supports HLS, is this something that sounds interesting? I kind of feel like such an API could only be necessary of MSE fails to solve all of the use cases it's supposed to handle, but I don't suppose that native support for HLS is going away, so...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
