    "created_at": "2016-06-30T16:12:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-30T16:12:51Z",
    "body": "There's no mechanism to manually switch variants in an HLS stream in iOS or macOS. You can detect resolution changes, and we do pipe that through to HTMLMediaElement's `videoWidth` and `videoHeight` properties, and we will now fire `resize` events when those values change. This should be testable in Safari Tech Preview, WebKit Nightlies, or Safari in the developer previews of iOS 10 or macOS Sierra.\n\nSee: https://trac.webkit.org/browser/trunk/LayoutTests/http/tests/media/hls/hls-video-resize.html.\n\nIf you're getting `resize` events but `videoWidth` isn't changing, please [file a bug](http://bugs.webkit.org) and we'll take a look. \n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
